From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:43:04 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 57/76] flashnext cuda: --pp 2 overlaps prompt chunks across
 the stages

A prompt chunk's rows return to rank 0 only when something there reads them:
its scores, the MTP head's streams or a keep; a bit in the forward frame tells
rank 1. Rank 0 posts the previous chunk's receive after its next front and
before its send, into a landing of its own, and the MTP head absorbs those
rows after the send. So rank 0's front of chunk c runs while rank 1 runs the
tail of chunk c - 1, with no grouped calls and the pass's rows untouched.

Rank 1's ack for such a chunk is read a chunk late; any other command first
takes the late rows and the ack. A lane released with rows still due drops
their absorb, not their receive. Kernels, chunk cuts and their order on each
rank are unchanged.
